<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Lower Bavaria</h1><p class="st-meta">1255 CE – 1340 CE · capital Landshut</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Wittelsbach duchy ruled from Landshut after the 1255 partition of Bavaria, whose duke Otto III was briefly King of Hungary.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the partition of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria</a> in 1255, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-xiii-duke-of-bavaria">Henry XIII</a> received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>, the lands along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isar">Isar</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inn-river">Inn</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> as residence. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-duke-of-bavaria">Louis II the Strict</a> took the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-upper-bavaria">Duchy of Upper Bavaria</a>. The two lines were often hostile.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trausnitz-castle">Burg Trausnitz</a> above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a>, relying on the estates, whose charter of 1311, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottonian-handfeste">Ottonian Handfeste</a>, gave them taxation rights. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-xiii-duke-of-bavaria">Henry XIII</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-iii-duke-of-bavaria">Otto III</a> was elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1305 but could not hold the throne. The duchy was repeatedly divided among co-rulers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Louis IV</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a> acted as guardian of its young dukes, defeating the Austrians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gammelsdorf">Gammelsdorf</a> in 1313.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the last Lower Bavarian duke, John I the Child, died in 1340, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Louis IV</a> inherited the duchy and reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a> later re-emerged as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a> and is now a district of Bavaria.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-lower-bavaria.jpg" alt="Duchy of Lower Bavaria" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lower_Bavaria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1255 CE – 1340 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Landshut</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry XIII of Bavaria, Otto III of Bavaria, Henry XIV of Bavaria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Niederbayern</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=duchy-of-lower-bavaria" aria-label="Duchy of Lower Bavaria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4962 481 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Lower Bavaria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5282 737L5279 723M5282 737L5291 727"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5279 723h0M5291 727h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5282 737h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5282 737h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Landshut. <a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=duchy-of-lower-bavaria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
